<title>SINGAPORE: NOL adds two ports to Gulf-Karachi route.</title>
<headline>NOL adds two ports to Gulf-Karachi route.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipping group Neptune Orient Lines Ltd (NOL) said on Monday it had added two new ports of call on its Gulf-Karachi express (GKX) route.</p>
<p>A consortium of NOL, Nippon Yusen Kaisha (NYK) and Peninsula and Oriental Steam Navigation Company (P&amp;O Containers), will add weekly calls at Port Klang, Malaysia, and Bahrain, to its schedule starting in January next year, a statement said.</p>
<p>The Port Klang call will offer shippers an end week direct sailing to the major Middle East ports.</p>
<p>And the addition of Bahrain will improve transits from the Far East and also improve export transits from Bahrain, it said.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65 870 3088)</p>
